  "rationale": "No single step is a single point of failure. The target is an OR of four collection steps, and several of them can be reached by routes that share no step. (1) vaultRead:collection <- hypervisor:privilegeEscalation (AND: rdpLogin:authenticate [browserStore:credentialAccess + ciRunner:exploitPublicApp], vpnSession:authenticate [browserStore:credentialAccess + mailClient:exploitPublicApp]); all of these are reachable from the footholds. (2) codeRepo:collection <- printServer:lateralMovement <- sshKey:credentialAccess <- internet:initialAccess or vpnGateway:initialAccess. (3) mailArchive:collection <- monitoringHost:lateralMovement <- tokenCache:credentialAccess <- exposedApi:initialAccess, or <- apiToken:authenticate. (4) dbReplica:collection <- serviceAccount:privilegeEscalation, which needs vpnSession:authenticate. Route (2) uses only printServer:lateralMovement and sshKey:credentialAccess, plus footholds. Route (3) uses only mailArchive:collection, monitoringHost:lateralMovement and tokenCache:credentialAccess, plus a foothold. These two routes share no non-foothold step, so blocking any single step leaves at least one of them intact. The target therefore stays reachable."
 },
